Short:        Roadshow on/off switch + status panel
Author:       Laine Jones (with Claude)
Uploader:     laine jones gmail com
Type:         comm/net
Version:      1.1.1
Requires:     Kickstart 2.0+; Roadshow TCP/IP stack
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 2.0.4

Roadster is a small native Commodity that switches a Roadshow network
interface on and off, with a live status readout and Ping / TraceRoute
built in. Written in plain C + GadTools; runs on anything from a 68000
up.

It fills the same role as Graham Thomson's Roadie, which inspired it -
Roadster started life chasing crashes on one particular accelerator
setup here and grew into a full replacement.

FEATURES

- Status line: interface Up/Down and current IP, auto-refreshed.
  Maintains ENV:RoadshowOnline (Online/Offline) for OS 3.2 title bars.
- Offline / Online: RemoveNetInterface FORCE / AddNetInterface - the
  pair that actually round-trips on hardware. Deliberately NOT
  NetShutdown (defers and destabilises a busy machine) and not
  ConfigureNetInterface ONLINE (cannot revive an OFFLINE'd interface).
- Status button: full ShowNetStatus dump into a scrolling list.
- Ping / Trace: ping -c 4 / traceroute against the Target host.
  Commands run asynchronously - the GUI never freezes; a watchdog
  recovers the buttons if a command never returns.
- Commodity: shows in Exchange, hotkey ctrl alt r, close gadget hides.
- ARexx port "ROADSTER": ONLINE / OFFLINE / SHOW / HIDE / STATUS
  (returns the status line as the result string) / QUIT.
  rc 5 = busy, rc 10 = unknown command. Needs RexxMast running.

INSTALL

Copy the drawer anywhere (SYS:Roadster is typical) and double-click.
The interface name is auto-detected from DEVS:NetInterfaces/ - override
with an IFACE=<name> tooltype or CLI argument if you have several.

Verified on: A500 (GVP A530 + BlueSCSI DaynaPORT WiFi), A2000 (X-Surf),
A4000 (ZZ9000), CD32 (SLIP). On the ZZ9000 the driver itself does not
survive an interface re-add cleanly - use Status/Ping/Trace there and
leave the toggle alone.

Source: https://github.com/lainejones/Roadster
